.el .ds Aq '
.TH urlmenu 1  "urlmenu 0.1.1" 
.SH NAME
urlmenu \- Pick a browser for each link, through your launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBurlmenu\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIURL\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pick a browser for each link, through your launcher
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print what would run as JSON instead of running it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIURL\fR]
URL or file to open. Without it, pick a browser to start
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
urlmenu\-list(1)
List detected targets with their ids and commands
.TP
urlmenu\-explain(1)
Show how a URL is cleaned, which rule or picker handles it, and its history; a fragment such as `github` lists every matching site
.TP
urlmenu\-items(1)
Print the menu as JSON, for an external picker
.TP
urlmenu\-open(1)
Open a URL (or nothing) with a target id from `list` or `items`
.TP
urlmenu\-copy(1)
Copy the cleaned URL to the clipboard
.TP
urlmenu\-forget(1)
Reset the picks remembered for a site, or for every site
.TP
urlmenu\-setup(1)
Register urlmenu as the default handler for http, https and HTML, and install shell completion. Without a part flag, does both
.SH VERSION
v0.1.1
